  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry weather will continue through the rest of the \nweek with a day to day warming trend.\n\nAn expansive area of high pressure will remain anchored over the \nOhio Valley and Great Lakes region this week. The axis of this \nsurface high is passing across our region this morning, with wind \nflow backing to more southwesterly, while also allowing for the \nwealth of upslope stratus this early morning to eventually diminish \nthrough the day. \n\nThis surface high will grant a partly to mostly sunny sky Wednesday \nand through the remainder of the week. Temperatures behind this \nsurface high, and with a stronger southerly flow, will rise back \nabove normal today, with several additional degrees tacked onto the \nhighs Wednesday and through the end of the week.",
